msgid "Sim-to-Real Strategy 4: Augmenting Datasets With Cosmos"
msgstr "Sim-to-Real 전략 4: Cosmos로 Dataset 증강"

msgid ""
"Cosmos Transfer demo showing an SO-101 input episode beside generated footage in a different "
"environment."
msgstr "SO-101 입력 episode와 다른 환경으로 생성한 영상을 나란히 보여주는 Cosmos Transfer demo입니다."

msgid "What Do I Need for This Module?"
msgstr "이 Module에 필요한 준비물"

msgid ""
"Lecture. You do not need a connected robot or a running container. Review the source and "
"generated videos, then discuss which variations would be useful for training."
msgstr "이론 수업입니다. 연결된 robot이나 실행 중인 container는 필요하지 않습니다. 원본과 생성 video를 검토하고 학습에 유용한 variation을 논의합니다."

msgid ""
"In this session, you'll explore Cosmos as an omnimodel for physical AI, then focus on one "
"application: creating diverse synthetic training data for robot policies. Source and generated "
"video examples illustrate which variations preserve useful training examples."
msgstr ""
"Physical AI용 omnimodel인 Cosmos를 살펴보고, robot policy 학습용 synthetic data 생성에 집중합니다. 원본과 생성 video를 통해"
" 어떤 variation이 유효한 training example을 보존하는지 확인합니다."

msgid "Learning Objectives"
msgstr "학습 목표"

msgid "By the end of this session, you'll be able to:"
msgstr "이 session을 마치면 다음을 수행할 수 있습니다."

msgid "**Explain** how Cosmos connects reasoning, world generation, and action modeling"
msgstr "Cosmos의 reasoning, world generation, action modeling 연결 방식 **설명**"

msgid "**Identify** where synthetic video augmentation fits in robot learning"
msgstr "Robot learning에서 synthetic video augmentation의 역할 **파악**"

msgid "**Assess** whether generated videos preserve the original task and motion"
msgstr "생성 video가 원래 task와 motion을 유지하는지 **평가**"

msgid "**Explain** how to test whether augmentation helps a policy"
msgstr "Augmentation이 policy에 도움이 되는지 시험하는 방법 **설명**"

msgid "Beyond Domain Randomization and Co-Training"
msgstr "Domain Randomization과 Co-Training을 넘어"

msgid ""
"In Strategy 1, you used domain randomization to vary configured simulation parameters. Generative"
" augmentation adds another way to vary scene appearance."
msgstr ""
"전략 1에서는 설정된 simulation parameter를 Domain Randomization으로 바꿨습니다. Generative augmentation은 scene "
"외관을 변화시키는 또 다른 방법입니다."

msgid ""
"For example, Cosmos 3 video transfer can use a source video and structural controls such as depth"
" or segmentation to generate visual variations. This complements the variations you create in the"
" simulator. [NVIDIA Cosmos 3 transfer "
"examples](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos/tree/main/cookbooks/cosmos3/generator/transfer)"
msgstr ""
"예를 들어 Cosmos 3 video transfer는 원본 video와 depth, segmentation 같은 structural control로 시각적 "
"variation을 생성해 simulator의 variation을 보완합니다. [NVIDIA Cosmos 3 transfer "
"examples](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos/tree/main/cookbooks/cosmos3/generator/transfer)"

msgid "What Is Cosmos?"
msgstr "Cosmos란?"

msgid ""
"**NVIDIA Cosmos** is a platform of world foundation models and tools for physical AI. **Cosmos 3 "
"is an omnimodel** that brings reasoning, world generation, and action generation into one "
"architecture. [NVIDIA Cosmos overview](https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai/cosmos/)"
msgstr ""
"**NVIDIA Cosmos**는 Physical AI용 world foundation model과 도구의 플랫폼입니다. **Cosmos 3는 omnimodel**로, "
"reasoning, world generation, action generation을 하나의 architecture에 결합합니다. [NVIDIA Cosmos "
"overview](https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai/cosmos/)"

msgid ""
"The Cosmos 3 family works across language, images, video, audio, and action sequences. Its "
"Mixture-of-Transformers architecture supports both understanding a scene and generating outputs "
"conditioned on that scene. [NVIDIA Cosmos 3 "
"documentation](https://docs.nvidia.com/cosmos/latest/cosmos3/index.html)"
msgstr ""
"Cosmos 3 family는 language, image, video, audio, action sequence를 다룹니다. Mixture-of-Transformers "
"architecture는 scene 이해와 해당 scene을 조건으로 한 output 생성을 모두 지원합니다. [NVIDIA Cosmos 3 "
"documentation](https://docs.nvidia.com/cosmos/latest/cosmos3/index.html)"

msgid ""
"Cosmos 3 omni-model architecture connecting an autoregressive text branch and a diffusion branch "
"for vision, audio, and actions through shared multimodal attention."
msgstr ""
"Shared multimodal attention으로 autoregressive text branch와 vision·audio·action용 diffusion branch를 "
"연결하는 Cosmos 3 omni-model architecture입니다."

msgid ""
"Cosmos 3 omni-model architecture, showing shared multimodal attention across autoregressive and "
"diffusion branches."
msgstr "Autoregressive 및 diffusion branch의 shared multimodal attention을 보여주는 Cosmos 3 architecture입니다."

msgid "For robot learning, these capabilities support several uses:"
msgstr "Robot learning에서는 다음과 같이 활용할 수 있습니다."

msgid "**Understand demonstrations:** reason about objects, interactions, and events in camera footage."
msgstr "**Understand demonstrations:** Camera 영상의 object, interaction, event를 추론합니다."

msgid ""
"**Generate training data:** create video variations and plausible future scenes from prompts and "
"other inputs."
msgstr "**Generate training data:** Prompt와 다른 입력으로 video variation과 가능한 미래 scene을 생성합니다."

msgid ""
"**Explore outcomes:** predict how a scene could evolve under different actions, supporting "
"planning and evaluation."
msgstr "**Explore outcomes:** 여러 action에 따라 scene이 어떻게 변할지 예측해 planning과 평가를 지원합니다."

msgid ""
"**Build policy models:** post-train a World Action Model (WAM), a model that connects "
"observations of the world to robot actions, using data for a particular robot and its cameras."
msgstr ""
"**Build policy models:** 특정 robot과 camera data로 world observation을 robot action에 연결하는 World "
"Action Model (WAM)을 post-train합니다."

msgid ""
"These uses follow [NVIDIA's Cosmos 3 capability overview](https://www.nvidia.com/en-"
"us/ai/cosmos/). This lesson focuses on data augmentation; the policy you train and deploy in the "
"workshop is GR00T 1.7."
msgstr ""
"이 활용 사례는 [NVIDIA Cosmos 3 capability overview](https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai/cosmos/)를 따릅니다. 이번"
" 실습은 data augmentation에 집중하며, 실제 학습·배포하는 policy는 GR00T 1.7입니다."

msgid "Read more about world prediction and action modeling"
msgstr "World Prediction과 Action Modeling 자세히 보기"

msgid ""
"**Forward dynamics** predicts what happens next from the current observations and proposed "
"controls. **Inverse dynamics** estimates actions that could explain a change between observed "
"states. A **robot policy** uses observations to choose actions for a task. NVIDIA demonstrates "
"these as different applications of Cosmos 3's shared model. [NVIDIA Cosmos 3 "
"research](https://research.nvidia.com/labs/cosmos-lab/cosmos3/)"
msgstr ""
"**Forward dynamics**는 현재 observation과 제안 control로 다음 상태를 예측합니다. **Inverse dynamics**는 관측 state "
"변화를 설명하는 action을 추정합니다. **Robot policy**는 observation으로 task용 action을 선택합니다. NVIDIA는 Cosmos 3의 "
"shared model로 이러한 서로 다른 활용을 보여줍니다. [NVIDIA Cosmos 3 research](https://research.nvidia.com/labs"
"/cosmos-lab/cosmos3/)"

msgid ""
"For an optional exploration, inspect the research examples and identify which inputs and outputs "
"each application needs. Then compare them with the wrist images, external images, joint states, "
"and actions in a workshop episode."
msgstr "선택적으로 연구 예시의 입력·출력을 확인하고 workshop episode의 wrist/external image, joint state, action과 비교해 보세요."

msgid "How Cosmos Works"
msgstr "Cosmos 동작 방식"

msgid ""
"Consider the video augmentation workflow below. Cosmos 3 uses a prompt and controls such as "
"edges, blur, depth, or segmentation to guide video generation. [NVIDIA Cosmos 3 transfer "
"examples](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos/tree/main/cookbooks/cosmos3/generator/transfer)"
msgstr ""
"아래 video augmentation workflow를 살펴보세요. Cosmos 3는 prompt와 edge, blur, depth, segmentation 같은 "
"control로 video generation을 유도합니다. [NVIDIA Cosmos 3 transfer "
"examples](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos/tree/main/cookbooks/cosmos3/generator/transfer)"

msgid "Source video, appearance prompt, structural control, and task-consistency review"
msgstr "Source video, appearance prompt, structural control, task-consistency 검토"

msgid "How Control Signals Shape the Result"
msgstr "Control Signal이 결과에 미치는 영향"

msgid "Control signals guide which parts of the source video Cosmos should preserve:"
msgstr "Control signal은 Cosmos가 원본 video의 어떤 부분을 보존할지 안내합니다."

msgid "**Edges** guide object outlines and positions."
msgstr "**Edges**는 object 윤곽과 위치를 안내합니다."

msgid "**Segmentation** separates regions such as the arm, rack, and vials."
msgstr "**Segmentation**은 arm, rack, vial 등의 영역을 나눕니다."

msgid "**Blur** provides the broad color and layout of the scene with less detail."
msgstr "**Blur**는 세부 묘사를 줄인 scene의 전체 색상과 배치를 제공합니다."

msgid ""
"Cosmos demo showing edge, segmentation, and blur inputs above a comparison of the real input with"
" edge-only, edge-plus-segmentation, and segmentation-only outputs."
msgstr ""
"위에는 edge, segmentation, blur 입력, 아래에는 real input과 edge-only, edge-plus-segmentation, "
"segmentation-only 결과를 보여주는 Cosmos demo입니다."

msgid ""
"The bottom row compares the real input with three generated results: edges only, edges plus "
"segmentation, and segmentation only."
msgstr "아래 행은 실제 입력과 세 가지 생성 결과(edges only, edges plus segmentation, segmentation only)를 비교합니다."

msgid ""
"Compare the rack holes, vial positions, and gripper shape. Which controls keep these details "
"closest to the source while still changing the appearance?"
msgstr "Rack hole, vial 위치, gripper 형태를 비교하세요. 외관을 바꾸면서도 원본의 세부 사항을 가장 잘 유지하는 control은 무엇인가요?"

msgid "Reference: reproduce a Cosmos 3 augmentation"
msgstr "참고: Cosmos 3 Augmentation 재현"

msgid ""
"Start with [NVIDIA's Cosmos 3 transfer notebook for "
"Diffusers](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos/blob/main/cookbooks/cosmos3/generator/transfer/run_video_transfer_with_diffusers.ipynb)"
" for setup and control-video examples."
msgstr ""
"설정과 control-video 예시는 [NVIDIA Cosmos 3 Diffusers transfer "
"notebook](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos/blob/main/cookbooks/cosmos3/generator/transfer/run_video_transfer_with_diffusers.ipynb)에서"
" 시작하세요."

msgid ""
"In one SO-101 trial, we prepared an edge-control video from an external-camera clip and prompted "
"Cosmos to change the surrounding laboratory. We used `nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano`, 121 frames at 640 × "
"480 and 30 FPS, 50 diffusion steps, prompt guidance 3.0, control guidance 1.5, and seed 2026. The"
" result also changed unintended objects, so compare each generated clip with its source before "
"using it for training."
msgstr ""
"SO-101 시험에서는 external-camera clip의 edge-control video를 만들고 주변 laboratory를 바꾸도록 prompt를 작성했습니다. "
"`nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano`, 640 × 480의 121 frame, 30 FPS, diffusion step 50, prompt guidance 3.0, "
"control guidance 1.5, seed 2026을 사용했습니다. 의도하지 않은 object도 변했으므로 학습 전에 생성 clip을 원본과 비교하세요."

msgid "Cosmos Augmentation Example 1"
msgstr "Cosmos Augmentation 예시 1"

msgid ""
"Two Cosmos restylings of the same robot episode: Pink World with a glittery pink mat and robot, "
"and Cartoon Workshop with bold colors and illustrated surroundings."
msgstr ""
"같은 robot episode를 glittery pink mat와 robot의 Pink World, 선명한 색상과 illustration 배경의 Cartoon "
"Workshop으로 바꾼 결과입니다."

msgid ""
"Cosmos can also make dramatic appearance changes: the same episode restyled as “Pink World” and "
"“Cartoon Workshop.” Notice how the robot, mat, and background change, then compare the vial and "
"gripper details."
msgstr ""
"같은 episode를 “Pink World”와 “Cartoon Workshop”으로 크게 바꿀 수도 있습니다. Robot, mat, background의 변화와 vial 및 "
"gripper 세부 사항을 비교하세요."

msgid "Example Dataset: Cosmos-Augmented Demonstrations"
msgstr "Dataset 예시: Cosmos-Augmented Demonstration"

msgid ""
"This [Cosmos Transfer "
"dataset](https://huggingface.co/datasets/bdelfino/so101_vials_dr_sts_250ep_20261005_CosmosTransfer)"
" restyles 10 simulation episodes to resemble physical footage, including a felt mat, foam rack, "
"and frosted vials. Both the external and wrist videos are augmented; the recorded states, "
"actions, and timestamps stay unchanged."
msgstr ""
"[Cosmos Transfer "
"dataset](https://huggingface.co/datasets/bdelfino/so101_vials_dr_sts_250ep_20261005_CosmosTransfer)은"
" simulation episode 10개를 felt mat, foam rack, frosted vial이 있는 실제 영상처럼 바꿉니다. External과 wrist "
"video를 모두 증강하되 기록된 state, action, timestamp는 유지합니다."

msgid ""
"External-camera excerpts from augmented dataset episodes 0, 4, and 9, showing the SO-101 moving "
"vials toward the rack."
msgstr "증강 dataset의 episode 0, 4, 9에서 SO-101이 vial을 rack 쪽으로 옮기는 external-camera clip입니다."

msgid "Excerpts from augmented episodes 0, 4, and 9, at normal speed."
msgstr "증강 episode 0, 4, 9의 정상 속도 발췌 영상입니다."

msgid ""
"Notice the vial caps, rack color, and gripper contact. Do they stay consistent as the arm moves? "
"The dataset author notes color drift and small geometry differences, and has not tested whether "
"these episodes improve a trained policy. See the [dataset "
"notes](https://huggingface.co/datasets/bdelfino/so101_vials_dr_sts_250ep_20261005_CosmosTransfer/blob/11418dc75d705a1d4ef1b8bcb66ea31b1cf386da/README.md)"
" for the source episodes and augmentation settings."
msgstr ""
"Vial cap, rack 색상, gripper contact가 arm 이동 중에도 일관되는지 보세요. 작성자는 color drift와 작은 geometry 차이를 "
"기록했으며, 학습 policy 개선 여부는 아직 시험하지 않았습니다. 원본 episode와 설정은 [dataset "
"notes](https://huggingface.co/datasets/bdelfino/so101_vials_dr_sts_250ep_20261005_CosmosTransfer/blob/11418dc75d705a1d4ef1b8bcb66ea31b1cf386da/README.md)를"
" 확인하세요."

msgid "What to Look for in Augmented Data"
msgstr "증강 Data 검토 기준"

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "**Visual Diversity**"
msgstr "**Visual Diversity**"

msgid "Photorealistic rendering variations"
msgstr "Photorealistic rendering variation"

msgid "Natural lighting changes"
msgstr "자연스러운 lighting 변화"

msgid "Background and texture diversity"
msgstr "Background와 texture 다양성"

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "**Scenario Variation**"
msgstr "**Scenario Variation**"

msgid "Background and surface changes"
msgstr "Background와 surface 변화"

msgid "Lighting variations"
msgstr "Lighting variation"

msgid "Appearance changes preserving recorded action labels"
msgstr "기록된 action label을 보존하는 외관 변화"

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "**Physical Consistency**"
msgstr "**Physical Consistency**"

msgid "Check that frames preserve task geometry"
msgstr "Frame이 task geometry를 보존하는지 확인"

msgid "Verify contact timing and motion against the source"
msgstr "Contact timing과 motion을 원본과 비교"

msgid "Reject augmentations that invalidate recorded actions"
msgstr "기록된 action과 맞지 않는 augmentation 제외"

msgid "Discussion: Assess Video Augmentation"
msgstr "토의: Video Augmentation 평가"

msgid "Use the source and generated examples above to discuss:"
msgstr "위 원본과 생성 예시로 다음을 논의하세요."

msgid "Which lighting, surface, or background changes would be useful for training?"
msgstr "어떤 lighting, surface, background 변화가 학습에 유용할까요?"

msgid "Do the vial positions, gripper shape, and contact timing still match the recorded actions?"
msgstr "Vial 위치, gripper 형태, contact timing이 기록된 action과 여전히 맞나요?"

msgid "Which examples would you keep or reject, and why?"
msgstr "어떤 예시를 남기거나 제외할 것이며 이유는 무엇인가요?"

msgid "How would you compare policies trained with and without augmented data to test whether it helps?"
msgstr "효과를 시험하려면 증강 data를 사용한 policy와 사용하지 않은 policy를 어떻게 비교할까요?"

msgid ""
"Reject examples that move the vial, change a grasp, or alter contact timing in a way that no "
"longer matches the recorded actions. This lecture uses prepared examples; running Cosmos "
"generation is not required."
msgstr ""
"Vial 이동, grasp 변경, contact timing 변화로 기록된 action과 맞지 않게 된 예시는 제외하세요. 준비된 예시를 사용하는 이 수업에서는 Cosmos "
"generation을 직접 실행할 필요가 없습니다."

msgid "Key Takeaways"
msgstr "핵심 내용"

msgid ""
"Cosmos 3 connects scene understanding, world generation, and action modeling; video augmentation "
"is one application."
msgstr ""
"Cosmos 3는 scene understanding, world generation, action modeling을 연결하며 video augmentation은 활용 사례 "
"중 하나입니다."

msgid ""
"Domain randomization, real demonstrations, and generative augmentation provide different ways to "
"expand training coverage."
msgstr ""
"Domain Randomization, 실제 demonstration, generative augmentation은 서로 다른 방식으로 training coverage를 "
"넓힙니다."

msgid "Inspect generated videos against the recorded actions before using them for policy training."
msgstr "Policy 학습 전에 생성 video와 기록된 action을 대조하세요."

msgid ""
"Compare policies on the same task to measure whether an augmentation mix improves real-world "
"performance."
msgstr "같은 task에서 policy를 비교해 augmentation 혼합이 실제 성능을 개선하는지 측정하세요."

